---

<!-- 释 -->
  <section id="glossary" style="position:relative;padding:96px 64px;background:transparent;border-top:1px solid var(--rulesoft)">
    <div class="section-mark section-mark-left" style="position:absolute;left:34px;top:120px;writing-mode:vertical-rl;color:var(--t4)">释</div>
    <div style="position:relative;z-index:1;max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto">
      <div style="position:absolute;top:-80px;left:54%;width:40%;max-width:480px;height:330px;z-index:-1;pointer-events:none;opacity:.5"><canvas id="tlGlossCanvas" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%"></canvas></div>
      <span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--teal)">Glossary</span>
      <h2 style="font-weight:700;font-size:42px;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-top:12px;color:var(--t1);max-width:760px">The review vocabulary stays narrow.</h2>
      <p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--t2);max-width:660px;margin-top:14px">These terms anchor the proof package. They keep the interface precise, especially when a human reviewer needs to audit how a verdict was reached.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:40px;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">
        <article class="gloss" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:280px 1fr;gap:40px;padding:26px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:16px">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="34" height="34" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px"><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="4" fill="var(--teal)"/><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="16" fill="none" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1"/><circle cx="31" cy="11" r="2.4" fill="var(--sand)"/></svg>
            <div><span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t4)">Noun</span><strong class="gw" style="display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:21px;color:var(--t1);margin-top:3px;transition:color .2s var(--ease)">Atomic claim</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--t2);align-self:center">A single proposition that can be checked independently. Telotia decomposes documents to this level before searching.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="gloss" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:280px 1fr;gap:40px;padding:26px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:16px">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="34" height="34" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px"><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="12" fill="rgba(47,111,176,.18)" stroke="var(--teal)" stroke-width="1.3"/><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="16" fill="none" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1"/><circle cx="31" cy="11" r="2.4" fill="var(--sand)"/></svg>
            <div><span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t4)">Noun</span><strong class="gw" style="display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:21px;color:var(--t1);margin-top:3px;transition:color .2s var(--ease)">Evidence base</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--t2);align-self:center">The corpus you supply and trust. Telotia checks claims against this, not the open web. You choose what counts as evidence.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="gloss" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:280px 1fr;gap:40px;padding:26px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:16px">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" width="34" height="34" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px"><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--teal)" stroke-width="1.3"/><circle cx="20" cy="20" r="16" fill="none" stroke="var(--rule)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 4"/><circle cx="31" cy="11" r="2.4" fill="var(--sand)"/></svg>
            <div><span style="font-family:var(--fmono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--t4)">Noun</span><strong class="gw" style="display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:21px;color:var(--t1);margin-top:3px;transition:color .2s var(--ease)">Decomposition</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--t2);align-self:center">Breaking a document into its individual atomic claims, each independently checkable. The first step before any search or grading.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
